        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Match the filter to the job and the rest of the machine looks after itself: <strong class="text-white">foam sleeve for water</strong>, <strong class="text-white">standard cartridge for chips and leaves</strong>, <strong class="text-white">fine dust or HEPA plus a bag for anything you would not want to breathe</strong>.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then fit a collection bag and keep a spare cartridge on the shelf. <strong class="text-white">The bag is the single highest-value accessory a shop vac has</strong> — it holds suction up through a job, multiplies filter life, and turns emptying from a dust cloud into lifting a sealed bag out of the drum.
          </p>
        </div>

